SUBJECT: Formal Submission of Proposal & Architecture Specification: BetGuard AI Integration

Dear Members of the Executive Leadership and Risk Committees,

As mobile wagering and high-frequency digital betting continue to scale across Botswana, maintaining operational efficiency while safeguarding platform integrity against emerging risk vectors—such as multi-accounting syndicates, bonus arbitrage, and account takeovers (ATO)—is a critical business imperative.

We are pleased to formally submit the enclosed technical proposal and architectural specification for BetGuard AI, an enterprise-grade, real-time risk scoring and compliance middleware built specifically for online gaming and sports betting operators.

Engineered to sit seamlessly between your web/mobile edge applications and your core Player Account Management (PAM) system, BetGuard AI delivers automated sub-150ms decisioning. By combining configurable business logic with an XGBoost machine learning engine compiled to an ONNX runtime, the platform offers several key operational benefits to Betway Botswana:

1. Automated Fraud Prevention: Instantly flags device reuse, syndicate registration patterns, and high-velocity withdrawal requests prior to payout execution.
2. Low-Latency Performance: Delivers median inference execution times under 35ms, preserving a frictionless experience for legitimate players.
3. Operational Efficiency: Reduces manual analyst review queue volume by up to 60%, allowing your fraud team to focus exclusively on high-priority investigations.
4. Regulatory Compliance: Integrates localized velocity tracking and responsible gaming flags to support ongoing compliance with Gambling Authority mandates.

The attached document package provides a comprehensive technical overview, including OpenAPI 3.0 REST/gRPC schemas, database models, ONNX runtime configurations, and Kubernetes deployment specifications.

We kindly request that this proposal package be forwarded to your Risk, Fraud, Technology, or Partnerships teams. We welcome the opportunity to schedule a brief 20-minute technical demonstration with your engineering and compliance leads.

Thank you for your time, consideration, and leadership.

Sincerely,

